{"step_index":90,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-08T12:05:57Z","content":"### Strategic, high‑quality “hands‑free” rollout plan  \n\nBelow is a **complete, automated pipeline** that will keep the NutraMEA front‑end in sync with the mobile‑friendly header you approved – *without any further manual steps from you*.  The solution assumes the site is hosted from a **Git repository** (the most common, production‑ready pattern) and that the server runs a standard CI/CD workflow (e.g., GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, or any other CI runner).  \n\nIf the NutraMEA code base already lives in a repo, simply point the pipeline at that repo.  If it does **not** yet exist, the first step creates the repo for you and pushes the initial code (including the updated `preview.html` / `nutrameiant_preview.html`).  After that, every time you (or any automation) updates the header file, the CI pipeline will rebuild and redeploy the site automatically.\n\n---\n\n## 1️⃣ Repository bootstrap (run once)\n\n```bash\n# ── 1. create a fresh repo (GitHub example) ────────────────────────\n# Replace <YOUR_ORG> and <REPO_NAME> with the target location.\ngh repo create <YOUR_ORG>/nutrameiant --public --source .\n# (If you prefer a private repo, add `--private`.)\n\n# ── 2. copy the mobile‑friendly HTML into the repo ─────────────────\nmkdir -p site\ncp /Users/riwana/.gemini/antigravity/brain/eb761f3c-fc89-4344-ad85-e44d64e83ea0/nutrameiant_preview.html site/index.html\n\n# ── 3. add a minimal static‑site server (optional) ─────────────────\ncat > site/package.json <<'EOF'\n{\n  \"name\": \"nutrameiant-site\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"build\": \"echo \\\"nothing to build – static site\\\"\",\n    \"start\": \"npx http-server ./ -p 8080\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"http-server\": \"^14.1.1\"\n  }\n}\nEOF\n\n# ── 4. commit & push ───────────────────────────────────────────────\ngit add site\n\n<truncated 3214 bytes>\nlect the new header **within minutes**, without you having to log into any admin console.\n\n---\n\n## 4️⃣ Optional “self‑healing” hook (extra robustness)\n\nIf you want the site to **self‑correct** should the header ever be overwritten, add a tiny GitHub Action that *re‑applies* the approved header on every successful deployment:\n\n```yaml\n- name: Ensure header integrity\n  run: |\n    # Grab the canonical header from the repository (stored in a separate file)\n    HEADER=$(cat ./site/header-snippet.html)\n    # Replace the header block in the generated HTML\n    perl -0777 -i -pe \"s|<header[^>]*>.*?</header>|$HEADER|gs\" ./site/index.html\n```\n\nPlace the canonical header in `site/header‑snippet.html`; the action rewrites the file **right before** the final publish step, guaranteeing that the production page always contains the exact markup you approved.\n\n---\n\n## ✅ What you get\n\n| Deliverable | Description |\n|-------------|-------------|\n| **`nutrameiant_preview.html` → `site/index.html`** | Mobile‑first header already in place. |\n| **CI pipeline (`.github/workflows/deploy.yml`)** | Fully automated build + deploy, no manual log‑ins. |\n| **Documentation** (this note) | Clear instructions for future contributors. |\n| **Extensibility** | Hook for asset optimisation, SASS compilation, etc., if the project grows. |\n\n---\n\n### Next step for you (one‑time)\n\n1. **Create the remote repository** (or tell me the existing repo URL).  \n2. **Add the SSH private key** (if you deploy to a custom server) as a secret named `SSH_PRIVATE_KEY` in the repository settings.  \n3. **Merge the CI file** (`.github/workflows/deploy.yml`) into the repo’s `main` branch.\n\nOnce those three items are in place, the pipeline runs **automatically** and the NutraMEA site will instantly serve the new mobile‑optimized header—no further human interaction required.  \n\nIf you prefer a different CI platform (GitLab, Bitbucket, Azure Pipelines, etc.), let me know and I’ll adapt the YA